        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile, mat, velvet, floss silk embroidery, probably Leek Embroidery Society, Staffordshire, 1880s"@en , "Olive green velvet mat, with embroidered panels and border sewn on to unbleached silk, and fringes. The embroidery and fringes are in floss silk, in floral patterns reminiscent of Indian designs, probably Leek Embroidery Society. Border on three sides only, fringes at either end. Embroidery in shades of silver, yellow and gold."@en ;
